== Graphic novel ==
{{distinguish|Moon Girl And Devil Dinosaur{{!}}Moon Girl And Devil Dinosaur (comic book)}}
On May 12, 2023, it was reported that a graphic novel based on the series was in development, entitled ''Wreck and Roll''. It was released on April 2, 2024.<ref name=":22">{{cite web|last=Johnston|first=Rich|url=https://bleedingcool.com/comics/moon-girl-devil-dinosaurs-wreck-and-roll-scholastic-graphic-novel/|title=Moon Girl & Devil Dinosaur's Wreck And Roll Scholastic Graphic Novel|date=May 12, 2023|website=[[Bleeding Cool]]|access-date=May 14, 2023|archive-date=May 14, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230514055237/https://bleedingcool.com/comics/moon-girl-devil-dinosaurs-wreck-and-roll-scholastic-graphic-novel/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite tweet|number=1657096110245126144|user=Steph_I_Will|title=This is based on the tv show!|author=herald of alien superstar|date=May 12, 2023|access-date=May 14, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Your First Look at the Cover to Original Graphic Novel 'Moon Girl and Devil Dinosaur: Wreck and Roll!' |url=https://www.marvel.com/articles/culture-lifestyle/first-look-preview-original-graphic-novel-moon-girl-and-devil-dinosaur-wreck-and-roll |access-date=2023-08-10 |website=Marvel Entertainment |archive-date=August 10, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230810230714/https://www.marvel.com/articles/culture-lifestyle/first-look-preview-original-graphic-novel-moon-girl-and-devil-dinosaur-wreck-and-roll |url-status=live }}</ref> The novel was written by [[Stephanie Williams (comics)|Stephanie Williams]] with art by Asia Simone, while [[Scholastic Corporation|Scholastic]] published it.<ref name=":22" />

